01:09:30.100 --> 01:09:30.620
Yeah.

01:09:30.820 --> 01:09:34.240
So this is a person whose whole life has been doing this work.

01:09:34.440 --> 01:09:34.640
Wow.

01:09:34.640 --> 01:09:42.460
Well, I think about the person you pseudonymously named Tyler in your book, and he's this NASA mission controller.

01:09:42.460 --> 01:09:46.700
It seems like he's using kind of consciousness protocols to make the launches work.

01:09:46.800 --> 01:09:48.180
He's this very interesting figure.

01:09:48.880 --> 01:09:52.960
But then he goes to the Vatican with you and he has this conversion experience.

01:09:52.960 --> 01:10:08.720
And it's almost as if what he looks into in the Vatican archives confirms that the work that he's been doing is somehow mystical and like way more like globally meaningful than just this nuts and bolts.

01:10:08.720 --> 01:10:11.080
Like we're putting satellites in space sort of thing.

01:10:11.520 --> 01:10:11.920
Yeah.

01:10:12.220 --> 01:10:12.280
Yeah.

01:10:12.280 --> 01:10:17.920
That was really an amazing experience for me to witness the conversion that he went through.

01:10:18.180 --> 01:10:28.020
We started at the Vatican looking at the records of Joseph of Copertino and a bilocating sister, Maria Vagrida.

01:10:28.500 --> 01:10:34.280
And we also had exposure to Peter Gumpel, who had been a papal advisor.

01:10:34.540 --> 01:10:35.220
He's a Jesuit.

01:10:35.720 --> 01:10:37.640
Talked a lot about the Templars, by the way.

01:10:38.340 --> 01:10:38.540
Yeah.

01:10:39.460 --> 01:10:41.460
Do you remember what he said about the Templars?

01:10:41.580 --> 01:10:41.920
I do.

01:10:41.920 --> 01:10:43.780
Um, okay.

01:10:44.380 --> 01:10:45.200
