01:10:56.760 --> 01:11:05.500
And I had a feeling that when we got to Castle Gandolfo at the Vatican Observatory, where he was going to meet astrophysicist monks.

01:11:05.500 --> 01:11:09.540
And, you know, those people that live like that, they have, you know, that's their mission.

01:11:09.780 --> 01:11:11.360
And their mission is fused.

01:11:11.540 --> 01:11:12.760
It fuses religion.

01:11:12.900 --> 01:11:13.480
And science.

01:11:13.700 --> 01:11:16.760
I knew that that would be his place.

01:11:16.940 --> 01:11:20.440
And that he would probably convert at that point.

01:11:20.480 --> 01:11:21.000
And I was right.

01:11:21.300 --> 01:11:23.520
So then we left the Vatican and we went there.

01:11:23.680 --> 01:11:32.120
And then he spent a lot of time in the archives looking at Copernicus and Kepler and, you know, originals, by the way.

01:11:32.300 --> 01:11:36.720
And also looking at electromagnetism.

01:11:37.040 --> 01:11:37.540
It's amazing.

01:11:37.700 --> 01:11:38.620
And things like that.

01:11:38.680 --> 01:11:41.280
And I just, like, couldn't get him out of the archives.

01:11:41.440 --> 01:11:42.680
Just, like, glued to these.

01:11:42.680 --> 01:11:43.380
To these books.

01:11:43.580 --> 01:11:44.160
It's incredible.

01:11:44.400 --> 01:11:48.760
And the other thing I wanted to follow up on from our first interview is you said this remarkable thing.

01:11:48.760 --> 01:11:51.540
